WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.800
Do you want to export your product to the EU,
but aren't certain what rules to follow?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.520
Then the EU Trade Helpdesk is the perfect tool for you!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.960
Here you'll find all you need to know about
the rules and regulations

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.640
and any customs duties you'll need to pay.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.120
Let`s say you want to export cocoa butter
from Ghana to France.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.400
First, select your product's country of origin.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.040
Then choose your destination country.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.960
Next, you'll need to find the EU product
code for cocoa butter.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.800
Simply click on “Find my product code”

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.800
and then type
"cocoa butter" in the “search” box.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.040
Once you've got your product code,

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.440
click on "search“

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.440
Now you'll see all the information about exporting cocoa butter
to the EU,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.080
separated into tabs:

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.000
First there is "import procedures".

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.360
This explains the customs procedures you'll need to follow;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.320
for example the paperwork you'll need to fill out.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.760
Second: "product requirements".

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.440
Here you'll find the health, safety and
technical standards

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.560
and the labelling rules for your product.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.360
Then, there is "import duties".

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.040
This will show you the duty you'll have to pay at customs

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.960
including any discount you might be eligible for.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:24.000
We also show you any other taxes that apply in the
EU country you're exporting to

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.200
as these affect the final price of your product.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.880
The "rules of origin" help us define the
"economic nationality" of your product

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.560
which is important when you claim a duty discount.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.360
And lastly,

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.680
you'll also find how much of your product the EU imports already

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.720
and from where

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.680
information you may need for your business plan.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.520
So, with the EU Trade Helpdesk and your
great product,

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.440
you'll have all you need to
crack the world's biggest market!

